  "notes": "Children start school on or after their 5th birthday; some schools record late starters as Year 0 before Year 1. Years 7-8 are taught at intermediate schools or at full primary schools (Years 1-8); the Ministry counts them as primary. Aliases Form 1-7 and Standard 1-4 are the older names, still heard. NCEA Levels 1-3 usually fall in Years 11-13."
